      "reason_summary": "Both historians agree on the core historical identity: '康' in Liu Xiaobiao's annotation refers to 嵇康 (Ji Kang), the subject of the main text entry. The disagreements are limited to (1) reference_type and (2) discourse.speaker_hint. Historian B's reference_type of 'personal_name' is more accurate than Historian A's 'surname_reference': the surface form is simply '康', which functions as an abbreviated personal name (shortened from the full name 嵇康), not a surname reference per se. Historian B also correctly identifies the speaker as 刘孝标 (Liu Xiaobiao), the annotator, since the text is within his annotation quoting the 康别傳. Historian A leaves speaker_hint empty, which is less informative. Historian B's record is therefore more complete and accurate on both disputed fields.",
